# Log2FC Bar Plot by Condition and Module R Script

This R script creates a diverging bar plot of Log2FC values for regulated proteins, grouped by functional module. Conditions are parsed into short labels (Lc, Li, Fv, Pb) and split by up/down regulation, with one row per protein × condition so the same protein's conditions stay adjacent.

The plot combines a main bar panel (colored by condition, faceted by regulation) with a left-side text strip showing each row's module assignment, aligned using `patchwork`. Row order is sorted by regulation → module → protein → condition.

## Input

- `Gv_regulated_modules_all.csv` with `condition`, `regulation`, `modules`, `protein`, and `Log2FC` columns.

## Output

- `plot3_bars_modules.pdf` (10×10 in).

## Requirements

R with `ggplot2`, `dplyr`, `readr`, and `patchwork`.

## Note

The condition palette is hardcoded for the eight Lc/Li/Fv/Pb × up/down combinations — adjust `cond_colors` and the `cond_key` factor levels if your conditions differ.

